<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
    Entitlements for a ``Lazy to Text.app`` signed with the local
    self-signed identity that scripts/setup-signing.sh creates — the
    build this repository makes today, on the machine that made it.

    Identical to scripts/entitlements.plist plus one key, and the one
    key exists for a measured reason rather than a precautionary one.

    The hardened runtime validates every library the process loads
    against the loading process's **Team ID**. A Team ID is issued by
    Apple; a certificate you generate yourself never has one, so every
    nested library here reports ``TeamIdentifier=not set`` and dyld
    refuses to match it to the executable. With the runtime on and
    only ``com.apple.security.device.audio-input`` declared, the
    inference worker dies on its first instruction:

        dyld: Library not loaded: @executable_path/../lib/libpython3.12.dylib
        Reason: tried: '…/Contents/Frameworks/libpython3.12.dylib'
          (code signature … not valid for use in process: mapping
          process and mapped file (non-platform) have different Team IDs)

    The window still opens, because the app falls back to the
    in-process backend — which is exactly how a dictation app that
    cannot paste looks from the outside: nothing fails, one feature is
    quietly gone.

    The alternative — putting the OU of a Team ID into the
    self-signed certificate — was tried and does not work:
    codesign still reports ``TeamIdentifier=not set`` for a
    certificate Apple did not issue. So the entitlement is the only
    route, and it is paid for only here.

    **A Developer ID build does not get this key.** Its nested code
    shares the bundle's Team ID, validation passes unaided, and
    scripts/build-macos.sh selects scripts/entitlements.plist for it.
    The protection is not turned off on the artifact that actually
    ships.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.device.audio-input</key>
    <true/>
</dict>
</plist>